)\n474:                            (some? (:origins state)) (assoc :origins (:origins state))\n475:                            (some? (:issued state)) (assoc :yin.k/issued (:issued state)))\n480:(defn rehydrate-fenced\n481:  \"Restore a version-2 export-recovery object into fresh receiver-owned\n498:   :machine m :record r}`, `r` marked `:recovered?` (abort refuses it).\"\n504:                  (true? (:yin.k/export-recovery recovery))\n505:                  (integer? (:yin.k/version recovery))\n506:                  (= 2 (:yin.k/version recovery))))\n513:        (let [pack-bytes (jing/base64->bytes (:yin.k/pack-bytes recovery))\n515:              state (:yin.k/state recovery)\n516:              baseline (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/pack-address recovery) pack-bytes)\n518:              wire (cbor/decode pack-bytes)\n550:                   (= (vec pack-bytes) (vec (:bytes reproduced))))\n563:(defn- not-appended?\n576:(defn abort\n589:   successor: it may abort only with `tenure`, `{:now n :bound b :live\n624:          prior (:gate record)]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PZSrFc5Hn8itDqpoxJ5L7m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzjVKP3yezRL8PAopGZG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013sQg2vbAsGa1n5MQP2Vfty","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc","offset":1,"limit":628},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3475,"cache_read_input_tokens":84662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3475},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24e59ef2-1e11-40bc-bf74-9b03c65bd1ca","uuid":"dd75c41f-c794-4cbb-94e7-52852a6b73b1","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:46:28.975Z","request_id":"req_011CfzjVK3xVZwsMHwJnq977","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013sQg2vbAsGa1n5MQP2Vfty":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc","offset":1,"limit":628}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013sQg2vbAsGa1n5MQP2Vfty","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.holder.export\n2\t  \"The exporting state of M-next D slice D8 (UCF 7.7.4; r3 1.8 and 1.9),\n3\t   over the row carrier since phase 7b: the holder side of a lift, over a\n4\t   machine value and data.\n5\t\n6\t   `enter` is the one-step transition into exporting: it sets\n7\t   `:yin.k/gate :exporting` on the root, requires an empty ready queue,\n8\t   and moves the wait set and every parked record into an export record.\n9\t   The machine then has nothing to poll, resume or advance, and the gate\n10\t   refuses what remains.  It refuses, as `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n11\t   `:reason-mismatch`, a task that holds (root or any install child) an\n12\t   `:observe` entry, any entry or cell carrying `:yin.k/held`, an\n13\t   unminted cursor cell, a pending close, or a `:link-request` entry\n14\t   whose response cursor is not installed.\n15\t\n16\t   `prepare` and `encode` are the split of r3 1.8, over `rows/lift-task`.\n17\t   Prepare calls the exporter's `serve!` once per stream (recursively for\n18\t   install children) and stores every answer in the record, keyed by\n19\t   task path and resource id (the lift's `:serve-keyed`); `encode` is a\n20\t   pure function of that record and the machine: it allocates and\n21\t   publishes nothing, and the same record gives the same canonical pack\n22\t   bytes.  The record retains the custody header and the composition's\n23\t   source index the lift ran under: code travels by A, and every carried\n24\t   A names its trees from that index (continuation §6.1).\n25\t\n26\t   `freeze` writes the export-recovery object, version 2: the published\n27\t   pack (its address, its root id, its bytes) beside the holder-local\n28\t   engine state the pack does not carry (gate, issue stamps, issued and\n29\t   origin counters, per task) and the header, whose enrolled set never\n30\t   travels.  The pack already carries the whole store, every parked\n31\t   record and every module store the tasks reach, so no second body is\n32\t   stored.  `rehydrate-fenced` restores it administratively through\n33\t   `rows/lower-task {:fenced true}` and proves the published pack is\n34\t   reproduced byte for byte.\n35\t\n36\t   `abort` returns the record to the machine only when the offer cannot\n37\t   have been admitted (7.7.4, r3 1.9).\n38\t\n39\t   Nothing here knows a transport, a driver or a journal.\"\n40\t  (:require [yin.vm :as vm]\n41\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n42\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n43\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n44\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint :as checkpoint]))\n45\t\n46\t\n47\t;; =============================================================================\n48\t;; Refusal data\n49\t;; =============================================================================\n50\t\n51\t(defn- non-portable\n52\t  [data]\n53\t  (assoc data\n54\t         :yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable\n55\t         :yin.k/kind :reason-mismatch))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(defn- refused\n59\t  [reason]\n60\t  {:yin.k/status :yin.k/refused :yin.k/reason reason})\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t;; =============================================================================\n64\t;; The tree of machines: the root and every install child\n65\t;; =============================================================================\n66\t\n67\t(defn- machines\n68\t  \"`[path machine]` of `vm` and, recursively, each install child, in\n69\t   install-name order of the map's own iteration.\"\n70\t  [path vm]\n71\t  (cons [path vm]\n72\t        (mapcat (fn [[m inst]]\n73\t                  (when (map? (:vm inst))\n74\t                    (machines (conj path m) (:vm inst))))\n75\t                (:installs vm))))\n76\t\n77\t\n78\t(defn- held-entry?\n79\t  [x]\n80\t  (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/held)))\n81\t\n82\t\n83\t(defn- refusal-at\n84\t  \"The first thing machine `m` holds that has no wire form, as the\n85\t   data the refusal carries, or nil.\"\n86\t  [m]\n87\t  (let [waits (:wait-set m)\n88\t        cells (filter map? (vals (:resources m)))]\n89\t    (cond\n90\t      (some #(= :observe (:reason %)) waits)\n91\t      {:yin.k/hold :observe}\n92\t\n93\t      (or (some held-entry? waits) (some held-entry? cells))\n94\t      {:yin.k/hold :held}\n95\t\n96\t      (some :yin.k/unminted cells)\n97\t      {:yin.k/hold :unminted-cursor}\n98\t\n99\t      (seq (:yin.k/closes m))\n100\t      {:yin.k/hold :pending-close}\n101\t\n102\t      (some #(and (= :link-request (:reason %)) (not (contains? % :cursor)))\n103\t            waits)\n104\t      {:yin.k/hold :link-cursor-not-installed})))\n105\t\n106\t\n107\t(defn- first-refusal\n108\t  [vm]\n109\t  (some (fn [[path m]]\n110\t          (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\n111\t            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/not-quiescent\n112\t             :yin.k/path path\n113\t             :yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\n114\t        (machines [] vm)))\n115\t\n116\t\n117\t;; =============================================================================\n118\t;; Entering exporting\n119\t;; =============================================================================\n120\t\n121\t(defn enter\n122\t  \"Enter exporting from `machine`.  Answers\n123\t   `{:status :ok :machine m :record r}`: `m` is `machine` with the gate\n124\t   `:exporting`, an empty wait set and no parked record, and `r` the\n125\t   export record, holding the wait set in order, every parked record\n126\t   (the row carrier carries them all, continuation §2.5), and the gate\n127\t   to return to.  Otherwise answers the data outcome of the first\n128\t   refusal, leaving `machine` as it was: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` for\n129\t   queued work in the root or a child, a `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n130\t   `:reason-mismatch` (naming the hold and the task path), or\n131\t   `:yin.k/refused` for a machine that is already exporting or ended.\"\n132\t  [machine]\n133\t  (cond\n134\t    (contains? #{:exporting :ended} (vm/gate-mode machine))\n135\t    (refused :not-running)\n136\t\n137\t    :else\n138\t    (or (first-refusal machine)\n139\t        (some (fn [[path m]]\n140\t                (when-some [h (refusal-at m)]\n141\t                  (non-portable (assoc h :yin.k/path path))))\n142\t              (machines [] machine))\n143\t        {:status :ok\n144\t         :machine (cond-> (assoc machine :yin.k/gate :exporting :wait-set [])\n145\t                    (contains? machine :parked) (assoc :parked {}))\n146\t         :record {:wait-set (vec (:wait-set machine))\n147\t                  :parked (:parked machine)\n148\t                  :gate (vm/gate-mode machine)\n149\t                  :served {}}})))\n150\t\n151\t\n152\t(defn- reinstated\n153\t  \"`machine`, an exporting machine, carrying `record`'s waits and\n154\t   parked records again: the value the lift reads.\"\n155\t  [machine record]\n156\t  (-> (reduce-kv (fn [restored module-name child-record]\n157\t                   (update-in restored [:installs module-name :vm]\n158\t                              reinstated child-record))\n159\t                 machine (or (:children record) {}))\n160\t      (assoc :wait-set (:wait-set record))\n161\t      (update :parked merge (:parked record))))\n162\t\n163\t\n164\t;; =============================================================================\n165\t;; Prepare, then encode\n166\t;; =============================================================================\n167\t\n168\t(defn- check-header!\n169\t  \"A header is nil (the fork lift) or a map carrying the arbitration,\n170\t   the counter and the enrolled set; anything else is a defect of the\n171\t   caller, not a refusal.  The lift judges the rest.\"\n172\t  [header]\n173\t  (when (some? header)\n174\t    (when-not (and (map? header)\n175\t                   (contains? header :yin.k/arbitration)\n176\t                   (contains? header :yin.k/next-op-seq)\n177\t                   (set? (:yin.k/enrolled header)))\n178\t      (throw (ex-info \"Prepare of a malformed header\"\n179\t                      {:yin.k/hint :malformed-header})))))\n180\t\n181\t\n182\t(defn- lift\n183\t  \"rows/lift-task of the record over `machine`, under the record's header\n184\t   and source index, every stream asked of `keyed`: `{:status :ok :wire\n185\t   w}` or the lift's refusal as data. A throw without the refusal\n186\t   vocabulary is a defect and propagates.\"\n187\t  [machine record keyed]\n188\t  (try\n189\t    {:status :ok\n190\t     :wire (rows/lift-task (reinstated machine record) nil\n191\t                           {:header (:header record)\n192\t                            :source-index (:source-index record)\n193\t                            :serve-keyed keyed})}\n194\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n195\t      (let [d (ex-data e)]\n196\t        (if (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d (throw e))))))\n197\t\n198\t\n199\t(defn- seeded-by-handle\n200\t  \"handle -> descriptor for every key the retained `table` already\n201\t   answers, resolved through `machine`'s own resource bindings at each\n202\t   key's task path: the alias reuse an interrupted prepare had already\n203\t   proved, reconstructed before any new key is served, so a retry never\n204\t   serves a handle the record already answers under another alias.\n205\t   Handles are never persisted; this mapping lives within the one\n206\t   call.\"\n207\t  [machine table]\n208\t  (let [at (into {} (machines [] machine))]\n209\t    (into {}\n210\t          (keep (fn [[[path id] descriptor]]\n211\t                  (when-some [h (get-in (get at path) [:resources id])]\n212\t                    [h descriptor])))\n213\t          table)))\n214\t\n215\t\n216\t(defn prepare\n217\t  \"Prepare `record`: call `serve!` once per stream of the exporting\n218\t   `machine`, install children included, and answer\n219\t   `{:status :ok :record r}` with every answer retained in `r`, or the\n220\t   data outcome of the lift's refusal with `:record` added, carrying\n221\t   what was served before the refusal so a retry never serves a stream\n222\t   twice -- not even under a resource alias the refused attempt never\n223\t   reached, whose handle the retained table and the machine's bindings\n224\t   still identify.  The row lift serves while it walks, so a refusal it\n225\t   decides after the walk (`:op-seq-exhausted`, `:unprotected-pending`,\n226\t   an op id on an unenrolled stream, the custody grammar) still finds\n227\t   the streams it reached served and retained (phase-7a D4).\n228\t\n229\t   The served table is keyed by `[task-path resource-id]` and holds the\n230\t   descriptor `serve!` answered. This table is plain data, but the live\n231\t   waits can contain authentic values: `freeze` is the persistence seam.\n232\t   A handle is asked at most once, across the calls of one retained\n233\t   record, even when two resources hold it.  `header` is nil for the\n234\t   fork lift, or the exclusive custody header (`rows/lift-task`'s\n235\t   `:header`), kept in the record as `:header`; `source-index` is the\n236\t   composition's `{A #{tree-address}}` (continuation §6.1), kept as\n237\t   `:source-index`.  Prepare mints nothing: the occurrence was minted by\n238\t   the driver before it was called.\"\n239\t  [machine record serve! header source-index]\n240\t  (check-header! header)\n241\t  (let [table (atom (:served record))\n242\t        by-handle (atom (seeded-by-handle machine (:served record)))\n243\t        once (fn [k h]\n244\t               (let [t @table]\n245\t                 (cond\n246\t                   (contains? t k)\n247\t                   (let [served (get t k)]\n248\t                     ;; an alias of an already-served key asks again for\n249\t                     ;; nothing: the handle is known served from here on\n250\t                     (swap! by-handle assoc h served)\n251\t                     served)\n252\t                   (contains? @by-handle h)\n253\t                   (let [served (get @by-handle h)]\n254\t                     ;; a handle already served under another resource id\n255\t                     ;; is the one stream: no second call, and the table\n256\t                     ;; must hold this key too or the record is unprepared\n257\t                     ;; for a resource it reached\n258\t                     (swap! table assoc k served)\n259\t                     served)\n260\t                   :else\n261\t                   (let [served (serve! h)]\n262\t                     ;; a refusal is not an answer: a retry asks again\n263\t                     (when (some? served)\n264\t                       (swap! table assoc k served)\n265\t                       (swap! by-handle assoc h served))\n266\t                     served))))\n267\t        record (assoc record :header header :source-index source-index)\n268\t        r (lift machine record once)]\n269\t    (if (= :ok (:status r))\n270\t      {:status :ok :record (assoc record :served @table)}\n271\t      (assoc r :record (assoc record :served @table)))))\n272\t\n273\t\n274\t(defn- kind-of\n275\t  \"The lifted task's kind, by the lift's own rule.\"\n276\t  [m]\n277\t  (let [value (:value m)]\n278\t    (cond\n279\t      (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value))\n280\t           (contains? (:parked m) (:id value))) :parked\n281\t      (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\n282\t      :else :halted)))\n283\t\n284\t\n285\t(defn encode\n286\t  \"The lift of the prepared `record` over `machine`, from a `serve-keyed`\n287\t   that only reads the record, under the header and source index the\n288\t   record retains: `{:status :ok :bytes b :address a :root B :kind k}`,\n289\t   `b` the pack's canonical bytes, `a` the pack address (BLAKE3 of `b`,\n290\t   the storage key), `B` the root id inside it; or the lift's refusal as\n291\t   data.  It allocates and publishes nothing, and one record gives equal\n292\t   bytes every time.  A stream the record has no answer for is a defect\n293\t   of the caller (an unprepared record), not a refusal.\"\n294\t  [machine record]\n295\t  (let [served (:served record)\n296\t        r (lift machine record\n297\t                (fn [k _h]\n298\t                  (if (contains? served k)\n299\t                    (get served k)\n300\t                    (throw (ex-info \"Encode of an unprepared record\"\n301\t                                    {:yin.k/hint :unprepared-stream})))))]\n302\t    (if (= :ok (:status r))\n303\t      (let [wire (:wire r)]\n304\t        {:status :ok\n305\t         :bytes (cbor/encode wire)\n306\t         :address (rows/pack-address wire)\n307\t         :root (:yin.k/root wire)\n308\t         :kind (kind-of (reinstated machine record))})\n309\t      r)))\n310\t\n311\t\n312\t;; =============================================================================\n313\t;; Freeze: the export-recovery object, version 2\n314\t;; =============================================================================\n315\t\n316\t(defn- recovery-address\n317\t  [bytes]\n318\t  (let [algorithm jing/default-hash-algorithm]\n319\t    (keyword \"segment\"\n320\t             (str (get-in jing/registry [algorithm :address-id]) \"-\"\n321\t                  (jing/digest-bytes algorithm bytes)))))\n322\t\n323\t\n324\t(defn- recovery-metadata\n325\t  \"The holder-local engine state of one task the pack does not carry:\n326\t   the gate to return to, each wait's issue stamp in wait order, the\n327\t   issued and origin counters, and each install child's, recursively.\"\n328\t  [machine record]\n329\t  {:gate (:gate record)\n330\t   :origins (:origins machine)\n331\t   :issues (mapv :yin.k/issue (:wait-set record))\n332\t   :issued (:yin.k/issued machine)\n333\t   :children (into {}\n334\t                   (map (fn [[module-name install]]\n335\t                          [module-name\n336\t                           (recovery-metadata\n337\t                             (:vm install)\n338\t                             (or (get-in record [:children module-name])\n339\t                                 {:gate (vm/gate-mode (:vm install))\n340\t                                  :wait-set (:wait-set (:vm install))}))]))\n341\t                   (:installs machine))})\n342\t\n343\t\n344\t(defn freeze\n345\t  \"The export-recovery object of the prepared record, version 2:\n346\t\n347\t     {:yin.k/export-recovery true\n348\t      :yin.k/version         2\n349\t      :yin.k/pack-address    a        ; the published pack's address\n350\t      :yin.k/root            B        ; the root id inside it\n351\t      :yin.k/pack-bytes      base64   ; the pack, byte for byte\n352\t      :yin.k/header          h        ; nil for a fork; the enrolled set\n353\t                                      ; stays here, never in the pack\n354\t      :yin.k/state           {:gate :origins :issued :issues :children}}\n355\t\n356\t   Answers `{:status :ok :bytes rb :address ra :pack-bytes b\n357\t   :pack-address a :root B :kind k}`, `rb` the recovery object's\n358\t   canonical bytes and `ra` their BLAKE3 address, or the encode's\n359\t   refusal.  Both objects must be stored durably before a fence is\n360\t   recorded.\"\n361\t  [machine prepared-record]\n362\t  (let [e (encode machine prepared-record)]\n363\t    (if (not= :ok (:status e))\n364\t      e\n365\t      (let [recovery {:yin.k/export-recovery true\n366\t                      :yin.k/version 2\n367\t                      :yin.k/pack-address (:address e)\n368\t                      :yin.k/root (:root e)\n369\t                      :yin.k/pack-bytes (jing/bytes->base64 (:bytes e))\n370\t                      :yin.k/header (:header prepared-record)\n371\t                      :yin.k/state (recovery-metadata machine prepared-record)}\n372\t            bytes (cbor/encode recovery)]\n373\t        {:status :ok :bytes bytes :address (recovery-address bytes)\n374\t         :pack-bytes (:bytes e) :pack-address (:address e)\n375\t         :root (:root e) :kind (:kind e)}))))\n376\t\n377\t\n378\t;; =============================================================================\n379\t;; Rehydrate: the fenced recovery\n380\t;; =============================================================================\n381\t\n382\t(defn- invalid!\n383\t  [data]\n384\t  (throw (ex-info \"Invalid export recovery\" (merge {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable} data))))\n385\t\n386\t\n387\t(defn- header-agrees?\n388\t  \"The recovery's header is the custody the pack's root slot carries:\n389\t   nil exactly for a fork; otherwise the slot's keys by kind (blocked or\n390\t   parked: occurrence, arbitration, counter and origin; halted: origin),\n391\t   a nil header value being an absent key, as the lift writes it.\"\n392\t  [header baseline]\n393\t  (if (nil? header)\n394\t    (true? (:yin.k/fork baseline))\n395\t    (let [ks (if (= :halted (:yin.k/kind baseline))\n396\t               [:yin.k/origin]\n397\t               [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin])]\n398\t      (and (not (:yin.k/fork baseline))\n399\t           (= (into {} (filter (comp some? val)) (select-keys header ks))\n400\t              (select-keys baseline ks))))))\n401\t\n402\t\n403\t(defn- counter?\n404\t  [x]\n405\t  (or (nil? x) (and (integer? x) (<= 0 x))))\n406\t\n407\t\n408\t(defn- valid-state?\n409\t  \"The recovery state fits the decoded task: one issue stamp per carried\n410\t   wait, and one child state per carried install, recursively.\"\n411\t  [task state]\n412\t  (let [ss (:slots task)\n413\t        installs (nth ss 12)\n414\t        waits (nth ss 13)]\n415\t    (and (map? state)\n416\t         (contains? #{nil :running :exporting :ended} (:gate state))\n417\t         (vector? (:issues state))\n418\t         (= (count (:issues state)) (count waits))\n419\t         (every? counter? (:issues state))\n420\t         (counter? (:issued state))\n421\t         (counter? (:origins state))\n422\t         (map? (:children state))\n423\t         (= (set (keys (:children state))) (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs))\n424\t         (every? (fn [inst]\n425\t                   (let [[mn _ _ _ child] (:slots inst)]\n426\t                     (valid-state? child (get-in state [:children mn]))))\n427\t                 installs))))\n428\t\n429\t\n430\t(defn- carried-trees\n431\t  \"{A #{tree}} every task of the decoded tree carries: the composition's\n432\t   index as the prepare that published the pack saw it, restricted to the\n433\t   carried segments, which is all a relift of the same tree reads.\"\n434\t  [task]\n435\t  (let [ss (:slots task)]\n436\t    (reduce (fn [acc inst] (merge acc (carried-trees (nth (:slots inst) 4))))\n437\t            (or (:yin.k/trees (nth ss 10)) {})\n438\t            (nth ss 12))))\n439\t\n440\t\n441\t(defn- extract-recovered\n442\t  \"The fenced machine and its export record from the lower's fenced\n443\t   restore of one task: the waits and parked records the lower kept out\n444\t   of the scheduler move into the record, the waits restamped with the\n445\t   recovered issues; the holder-local counters come from `state`.\"\n446\t  [machine state]\n447\t  (let [children (into {}\n448\t                       (map (fn [[module-name install]]\n449\t                              [module-name\n450\t                               (extract-recovered (:vm install)\n451\t                                                  (get-in state [:children module-name]))]))\n452\t                       (:installs machine))\n453\t        waits (mapv (fn [entry issue]\n454\t                      (if (some? issue)\n455\t                        (assoc entry :yin.k/issue issue)\n456\t                        (dissoc entry :yin.k/issue)))\n457\t                    (:yin.k/recovery-waits machine)\n458\t                    (:issues state))\n459\t        record {:wait-set waits\n460\t                :parked (or (:yin.k/recovery-parked machine) {})\n461\t                :recovered? true\n462\t                :gate (:gate state)\n463\t                :served {}\n464\t                :children (into {} (map (fn [[module-name recovered]]\n465\t                                          [module-name (:record recovered)]))\n466\t                                children)}\n467\t        fenced (reduce-kv (fn [parent module-name recovered]\n468\t                            (assoc-in parent [:installs module-name :vm]\n469\t                                      (:machine recovered)))\n470\t                          (cond-> (-> machine\n471\t                                      (dissoc :yin.k/recovery-waits :yin.k/recovery-parked\n472\t                                              :yin.k/custody :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued :origins)\n473\t                                      (assoc :wait-set [] :parked {} :yin.k/gate :exporting))\n474\t                            (some? (:origins state)) (assoc :origins (:origins state))\n475\t                            (some? (:issued state)) (assoc :yin.k/issued (:issued state)))\n476\t                          children)]\n477\t    {:machine fenced :record record}))\n478\t\n479\t\n480\t(defn rehydrate-fenced\n481\t  \"Restore a version-2 export-recovery object into fresh receiver-owned\n482\t   values (UCF 7.7.4).  Before any attachment: the object's tag and\n483\t   version (`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`), its bytes against `address`\n484\t   (`:yin.k/hash-mismatch`), the pack through the rows inspector (its\n485\t   address against its bytes, the carrier, the custody grammar), the pack\n486\t   root against the object's, the header against the root's custody\n487\t   slot, and the state against the carried tree (any of these\n488\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`, or the inspector's own refusal).  Then\n489\t   `rows/lower-task {:fenced true}` over `receiver`, `attach` once per\n490\t   stream identity: every task stays exporting, its waits and parked\n491\t   records outside the scheduler and in the record, its id counter\n492\t   exact; no program code runs, no stream is read, written, minted or\n493\t   closed, no install child initializes.  Never restores tenure,\n494\t   custody, scheduler waits or a runnable gate.  Last, the recovered\n495\t   record is prepared again from what was attached and must encode the\n496\t   published pack byte for byte, or the answer is `:yin.k/undecodable`\n497\t   with `:yin.k/reason :recovery-inconsistent`.  Answers `{:status :ok\n498\t   :machine m :record r}`, `r` marked `:recovered?` (abort refuses it).\"\n499\t  [receiver recovery-bytes {:keys [address attach]}]\n500\t  (try\n501\t    (let [recovery (cbor/decode recovery-bytes)]\n502\t      (cond\n503\t        (not (and (map? recovery)\n504\t                  (true? (:yin.k/export-recovery recovery))\n505\t                  (integer? (:yin.k/version recovery))\n506\t                  (= 2 (:yin.k/version recovery))))\n507\t        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/profile-mismatch}\n508\t\n509\t        (not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address recovery-bytes))\n510\t        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/hash-mismatch}\n511\t\n512\t        :else\n513\t        (let [pack-bytes (jing/base64->bytes (:yin.k/pack-bytes recovery))\n514\t              header (:yin.k/header recovery)\n515\t              state (:yin.k/state recovery)\n516\t              baseline (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/pack-address recovery) pack-bytes)\n517\t              _ (when (:yin.k/status baseline) (invalid! baseline))\n518\t              wire (cbor/decode pack-bytes)\n519\t              task (rows/decode wire)\n520\t              _ (when-not (= (:yin.k/root recovery) (:yin.k/root baseline))\n521\t                  (invalid! {:yin.k/reason :root}))\n522\t              _ (check-header! header)\n523\t              _ (when-not (header-agrees? header baseline)\n524\t                  (invalid! {:yin.k/reason :header}))\n525\t              _ (when-not (valid-state? task state)\n526\t                  (invalid! {:yin.k/reason :state}))\n527\t              attached (atom {})\n528\t              restored (rows/lower-task\n529\t                         receiver wire\n530\t                         (fn [descriptor]\n531\t                           (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity descriptor)]\n532\t                             (if (contains? @attached identity)\n533\t                               (:answer (get @attached identity))\n534\t                               (let [answer (attach descriptor)]\n535\t                                 (swap! attached assoc identity {:answer answer :descriptor descriptor})\n536\t                                 answer))))\n537\t                         {:fenced true})\n538\t              {:keys [machine record]} (extract-recovered restored state)\n539\t              ;; each attached handle answers the descriptor it was served under\n540\t              by-handle (into {}\n541\t                              (map (fn [{:keys [answer descriptor]}]\n542\t                                     [(:dao.stream/handle answer)\n543\t                                      (select-keys descriptor [:dao.stream/identity\n544\t                                                               :dao.stream/channel])]))\n545\t                              (vals @attached))\n546\t              prepared (prepare machine record #(get by-handle %) header (carried-trees task))\n547\t              reproduced (when (= :ok (:status prepared))\n548\t                           (encode machine (:record prepared)))]\n549\t          (if (and (= :ok (:status reproduced))\n550\t                   (= (vec pack-bytes) (vec (:bytes reproduced))))\n551\t            {:status :ok :machine machine :record (assoc (:record prepared) :recovered? true)}\n552\t            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable\n553\t             :yin.k/reason :recovery-inconsistent}))))\n554\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) failure\n555\t      (or (when (:yin.k/status (ex-data failure)) (ex-data failure))\n556\t          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable}))))\n557\t\n558\t\n559\t;; =============================================================================\n560\t;; Abort\n561\t;; =============================================================================\n562\t\n563\t(defn- not-appended?\n564\t  \"True when `outcome`, the answer of an offer attempt's append, proves\n565\t   the value was not appended.  `dao.stream`'s closed append outcome\n566\t   set is {ok full invalid-value closed refused transport-error}: the\n567\t   four refusals prove it; `ok` proves the opposite, and\n568\t   `transport-error` stays the unknown-delivery refusal, as does no\n569\t   answer.\"\n570\t  [outcome]\n571\t  (contains? #{:dao.stream/full :dao.stream/invalid-value\n572\t               :dao.stream/closed :dao.stream/refused}\n573\t             outcome))\n574\t\n575\t\n576\t(defn abort\n577\t  \"Return the exporting `machine` to local execution from `record`.\n578\t\n579\t   `attempts` is the offer-attempt history the composition persisted:\n580\t   one map per attempt whose intent was durable before the send, with\n581\t   `:append` the outcome its append answered (absent when none did).\n582\t   Abort is legal when there is no attempt, or when every attempt's\n583\t   append proves the value was not appended; anything else, including\n584\t   an authority's refusal of one attempt, leaves the source fenced.  A\n585\t   recovered record (`rehydrate-fenced`) is refused `:restarted`: a\n586\t   restart never hands execution back.\n587\t\n588\t   A machine under custody (`:yin.k/custody`) is a holder exporting a\n589\t   successor: it may abort only with `tenure`, `{:now n :bound b :live\n590\t   true}`: `n` before `b` in one unit, and `:live` the ledger reader's\n591\t   evidence that this lease is the occurrence's active lease at its\n592\t   epoch.  A clock reading alone is not tenure.  After the lease has\n593\t   ended its old local machine is never restored.\n594\t\n595\t   Answers `{:status :ok :machine m}` or `:yin.k/refused` data with\n596\t   reason `:restarted`, `:not-exporting`, `:tenure-ended` (at or past\n597\t   the bound), `:tenure-unconfirmed` (no ledger evidence) or\n598\t   `:offer-possibly-accepted`.\"\n599\t  [machine record attempts tenure]\n600\t  (cond\n601\t    (:recovered? record)\n602\t    (refused :restarted)\n603\t\n604\t    (not= :exporting (vm/gate-mode machine))\n605\t    (refused :not-exporting)\n606\t\n607\t    (and (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n608\t         (some? (:now tenure))\n609\t         (some? (:bound tenure))\n610\t         (>= (:now tenure) (:bound tenure)))\n611\t    (refused :tenure-ended)\n612\t\n613\t    (and (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n614\t         (not (and (some? (:now tenure))\n615\t                   (some? (:bound tenure))\n616\t                   (true? (:live tenure)))))\n617\t    (refused :tenure-unconfirmed)\n618\t\n619\t    (not (every? (comp not-appended? :append) attempts))\n620\t    (refused :offer-possibly-accepted)\n621\t\n622\t    :else\n623\t    (let [m (reinstated machine record)\n624\t          prior (:gate record)]\n625\t      {:status :ok\n626\t       :machine (if (some? prior)\n627\t                  (assoc m :yin.k/gate prior)\n628\t                  (dissoc m :yin.k/gate))})))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24e59ef2-1e11-40bc-bf74-9b03c65bd1ca","uuid":"402309c0-6dfb-45fd-82e9-2b182b759ab1","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:46:29.350Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.holder.export\n  \"The exporting state of M-next D slice D8 (UCF 7.7.4; r3 1.8 and 1.9),\n   over the row carrier since phase 7b: the holder side of a lift, over a\n   machine value and data.\n\n   `enter` is the one-step transition into exporting: it sets\n   `:yin.k/gate :exporting` on the root, requires an empty ready queue,\n   and moves the wait set and every parked record into an export record.\n   The machine then has nothing to poll, resume or advance, and the gate\n   refuses what remains.  It refuses, as `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n   `:reason-mismatch`, a task that holds (root or any install child) an\n   `:observe` entry, any entry or cell carrying `:yin.k/held`, an\n   unminted cursor cell, a pending close, or a `:link-request` entry\n   whose response cursor is not installed.\n\n   `prepare` and `encode` are the split of r3 1.8, over `rows/lift-task`.\n   Prepare calls the exporter's `serve!` once per stream (recursively for\n   install children) and stores every answer in the record, keyed by\n   task path and resource id (the lift's `:serve-keyed`); `encode` is a\n   pure function of that record and the machine: it allocates and\n   publishes nothing, and the same record gives the same canonical pack\n   bytes.  The record retains the custody header and the composition's\n   source index the lift ran under: code travels by A, and every carried\n   A names its trees from that index (continuation §6.1).\n\n   `freeze` writes the export-recovery object, version 2: the published\n   pack (its address, its root id, its bytes) beside the holder-local\n   engine state the pack does not carry (gate, issue stamps, issued and\n   origin counters, per task) and the header, whose enrolled set never\n   travels.  The pack already carries the whole store, every parked\n   record and every module store the tasks reach, so no second body is\n   stored.  `rehydrate-fenced` restores it administratively through\n   `rows/lower-task {:fenced true}` and proves the published pack is\n   reproduced byte for byte.\n\n   `abort` returns the record to the machine only when the offer cannot\n   have been admitted (7.7.4, r3 1.9).\n\n   Nothing here knows a transport, a driver or a journal.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint :as checkpoint]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Refusal data\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- non-portable\n  [data]\n  (assoc data\n         :yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable\n         :yin.k/kind :reason-mismatch))\n\n\n(defn- refused\n  [reason]\n  {:yin.k/status :yin.k/refused :yin.k/reason reason})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The tree of machines: the root and every install child\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- machines\n  \"`[path machine]` of `vm` and, recursively, each install child, in\n   install-name order of the map's own iteration.\"\n  [path vm]\n  (cons [path vm]\n        (mapcat (fn [[m inst]]\n                  (when (map? (:vm inst))\n                    (machines (conj path m) (:vm inst))))\n                (:installs vm))))\n\n\n(defn- held-entry?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/held)))\n\n\n(defn- refusal-at\n  \"The first thing machine `m` holds that has no wire form, as the\n   data the refusal carries, or nil.\"\n  [m]\n  (let [waits (:wait-set m)\n        cells (filter map? (vals (:resources m)))]\n    (cond\n      (some #(= :observe (:reason %)) waits)\n      {:yin.k/hold :observe}\n\n      (or (some held-entry? waits) (some held-entry? cells))\n      {:yin.k/hold :held}\n\n      (some :yin.k/unminted cells)\n      {:yin.k/hold :unminted-cursor}\n\n      (seq (:yin.k/closes m))\n      {:yin.k/hold :pending-close}\n\n      (some #(and (= :link-request (:reason %)) (not (contains? % :cursor)))\n            waits)\n      {:yin.k/hold :link-cursor-not-installed})))\n\n\n(defn- first-refusal\n  [vm]\n  (some (fn [[path m]]\n          (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\n            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/not-quiescent\n             :yin.k/path path\n             :yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\n        (machines [] vm)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Entering exporting\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn enter\n  \"Enter exporting from `machine`.  Answers\n   `{:status :ok :machine m :record r}`: `m` is `machine` with the gate\n   `:exporting`, an empty wait set and no parked record, and `r` the\n   export record, holding the wait set in order, every parked record\n   (the row carrier carries them all, continuation §2.5), and the gate\n   to return to.  Otherwise answers the data outcome of the first\n   refusal, leaving `machine` as it was: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` for\n   queued work in the root or a child, a `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n   `:reason-mismatch` (naming the hold and the task path), or\n   `:yin.k/refused` for a machine that is already exporting or ended.\"\n  [machine]\n  (cond\n    (contains? #{:exporting :ended} (vm/gate-mode machine))\n    (refused :not-running)\n\n    :else\n    (or (first-refusal machine)\n        (some (fn [[path m]]\n                (when-some [h (refusal-at m)]\n                  (non-portable (assoc h :yin.k/path path))))\n              (machines [] machine))\n        {:status :ok\n         :machine (cond-> (assoc machine :yin.k/gate :exporting :wait-set [])\n                    (contains? machine :parked) (assoc :parked {}))\n         :record {:wait-set (vec (:wait-set machine))\n                  :parked (:parked machine)\n                  :gate (vm/gate-mode machine)\n                  :served {}}})))\n\n\n(defn- reinstated\n  \"`machine`, an exporting machine, carrying `record`'s waits and\n   parked records again: the value the lift reads.\"\n  [machine record]\n  (-> (reduce-kv (fn [restored module-name child-record]\n                   (update-in restored [:installs module-name :vm]\n                              reinstated child-record))\n                 machine (or (:children record) {}))\n      (assoc :wait-set (:wait-set record))\n      (update :parked merge (:parked record))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Prepare, then encode\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- check-header!\n  \"A header is nil (the fork lift) or a map carrying the arbitration,\n   the counter and the enrolled set; anything else is a defect of the\n   caller, not a refusal.  The lift judges the rest.\"\n  [header]\n  (when (some? header)\n    (when-not (and (map? header)\n                   (contains? header :yin.k/arbitration)\n                   (contains? header :yin.k/next-op-seq)\n                   (set? (:yin.k/enrolled header)))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Prepare of a malformed header\"\n                      {:yin.k/hint :malformed-header})))))\n\n\n(defn- lift\n  \"rows/lift-task of the record over `machine`, under the record's header\n   and source index, every stream asked of `keyed`: `{:status :ok :wire\n   w}` or the lift's refusal as data. A throw without the refusal\n   vocabulary is a defect and propagates.\"\n  [machine record keyed]\n  (try\n    {:status :ok\n     :wire (rows/lift-task (reinstated machine record) nil\n                           {:header (:header record)\n                            :source-index (:source-index record)\n                            :serve-keyed keyed})}\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n      (let [d (ex-data e)]\n        (if (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn- seeded-by-handle\n  \"handle -> descriptor for every key the retained `table` already\n   answers, resolved through `machine`'s own resource bindings at each\n   key's task path: the alias reuse an interrupted prepare had already\n   proved, reconstructed before any new key is served, so a retry never\n   serves a handle the record already answers under another alias.\n   Handles are never persisted; this mapping lives within the one\n   call.\"\n  [machine table]\n  (let [at (into {} (machines [] machine))]\n    (into {}\n          (keep (fn [[[path id] descriptor]]\n                  (when-some [h (get-in (get at path) [:resources id])]\n                    [h descriptor])))\n          table)))\n\n\n(defn prepare\n  \"Prepare `record`: call `serve!` once per stream of the exporting\n   `machine`, install children included, and answer\n   `{:status :ok :record r}` with every answer retained in `r`, or the\n   data outcome of the lift's refusal with `:record` added, carrying\n   what was served before the refusal so a retry never serves a stream\n   twice -- not even under a resource alias the refused attempt never\n   reached, whose handle the retained table and the machine's bindings\n   still identify.  The row lift serves while it walks, so a refusal it\n   decides after the walk (`:op-seq-exhausted`, `:unprotected-pending`,\n   an op id on an unenrolled stream, the custody grammar) still finds\n   the streams it reached served and retained (phase-7a D4).\n\n   The served table is keyed by `[task-path resource-id]` and holds the\n   descriptor `serve!` answered. This table is plain data, but the live\n   waits can contain authentic values: `freeze` is the persistence seam.\n   A handle is asked at most once, across the calls of one retained\n   record, even when two resources hold it.  `header` is nil for the\n   fork lift, or the exclusive custody header (`rows/lift-task`'s\n   `:header`), kept in the record as `:header`; `source-index` is the\n   composition's `{A #{tree-address}}` (continuation §6.1), kept as\n   `:source-index`.  Prepare mints nothing: the occurrence was minted by\n   the driver before it was called.\"\n  [machine record serve! header source-index]\n  (check-header! header)\n  (let [table (atom (:served record))\n        by-handle (atom (seeded-by-handle machine (:served record)))\n        once (fn [k h]\n               (let [t @table]\n                 (cond\n                   (contains? t k)\n                   (let [served (get t k)]\n                     ;; an alias of an already-served key asks again for\n                     ;; nothing: the handle is known served from here on\n                     (swap! by-handle assoc h served)\n                     served)\n                   (contains? @by-handle h)\n                   (let [served (get @by-handle h)]\n                     ;; a handle already served under another resource id\n                     ;; is the one stream: no second call, and the table\n                     ;; must hold this key too or the record is unprepared\n                     ;; for a resource it reached\n                     (swap! table assoc k served)\n                     served)\n                   :else\n                   (let [served (serve! h)]\n                     ;; a refusal is not an answer: a retry asks again\n                     (when (some? served)\n                       (swap! table assoc k served)\n                       (swap! by-handle assoc h served))\n                     served))))\n        record (assoc record :header header :source-index source-index)\n        r (lift machine record once)]\n    (if (= :ok (:status r))\n      {:status :ok :record (assoc record :served @table)}\n      (assoc r :record (assoc record :served @table)))))\n\n\n(defn- kind-of\n  \"The lifted task's kind, by the lift's own rule.\"\n  [m]\n  (let [value (:value m)]\n    (cond\n      (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value))\n           (contains? (:parked m) (:id value))) :parked\n      (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\n      :else :halted)))\n\n\n(defn encode\n  \"The lift of the prepared `record` over `machine`, from a `serve-keyed`\n   that only reads the record, under the header and source index the\n   record retains: `{:status :ok :bytes b :address a :root B :kind k}`,\n   `b` the pack's canonical bytes, `a` the pack address (BLAKE3 of `b`,\n   the storage key), `B` the root id inside it; or the lift's refusal as\n   data.  It allocates and publishes nothing, and one record gives equal\n   bytes every time.  A stream the record has no answer for is a defect\n   of the caller (an unprepared record), not a refusal.\"\n  [machine record]\n  (let [served (:served record)\n        r (lift machine record\n                (fn [k _h]\n                  (if (contains? served k)\n                    (get served k)\n                    (throw (ex-info \"Encode of an unprepared record\"\n                                    {:yin.k/hint :unprepared-stream})))))]\n    (if (= :ok (:status r))\n      (let [wire (:wire r)]\n        {:status :ok\n         :bytes (cbor/encode wire)\n         :address (rows/pack-address wire)\n         :root (:yin.k/root wire)\n         :kind (kind-of (reinstated machine record))})\n      r)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Freeze: the export-recovery object, version 2\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- recovery-address\n  [bytes]\n  (let [algorithm jing/default-hash-algorithm]\n    (keyword \"segment\"\n             (str (get-in jing/registry [algorithm :address-id]) \"-\"\n                  (jing/digest-bytes algorithm bytes)))))\n\n\n(defn- recovery-metadata\n  \"The holder-local engine state of one task the pack does not carry:\n   the gate to return to, each wait's issue stamp in wait order, the\n   issued and origin counters, and each install child's, recursively.\"\n  [machine record]\n  {:gate (:gate record)\n   :origins (:origins machine)\n   :issues (mapv :yin.k/issue (:wait-set record))\n   :issued (:yin.k/issued machine)\n   :children (into {}\n                   (map (fn [[module-name install]]\n                          [module-name\n                           (recovery-metadata\n                             (:vm install)\n                             (or (get-in record [:children module-name])\n                                 {:gate (vm/gate-mode (:vm install))\n                                  :wait-set (:wait-set (:vm install))}))]))\n                   (:installs machine))})\n\n\n(defn freeze\n  \"The export-recovery object of the prepared record, version 2:\n\n     {:yin.k/export-recovery true\n      :yin.k/version         2\n      :yin.k/pack-address    a        ; the published pack's address\n      :yin.k/root            B        ; the root id inside it\n      :yin.k/pack-bytes      base64   ; the pack, byte for byte\n      :yin.k/header          h        ; nil for a fork; the enrolled set\n                                      ; stays here, never in the pack\n      :yin.k/state           {:gate :origins :issued :issues :children}}\n\n   Answers `{:status :ok :bytes rb :address ra :pack-bytes b\n   :pack-address a :root B :kind k}`, `rb` the recovery object's\n   canonical bytes and `ra` their BLAKE3 address, or the encode's\n   refusal.  Both objects must be stored durably before a fence is\n   recorded.\"\n  [machine prepared-record]\n  (let [e (encode machine prepared-record)]\n    (if (not= :ok (:status e))\n      e\n      (let [recovery {:yin.k/export-recovery true\n                      :yin.k/version 2\n                      :yin.k/pack-address (:address e)\n                      :yin.k/root (:root e)\n                      :yin.k/pack-bytes (jing/bytes->base64 (:bytes e))\n                      :yin.k/header (:header prepared-record)\n                      :yin.k/state (recovery-metadata machine prepared-record)}\n            bytes (cbor/encode recovery)]\n        {:status :ok :bytes bytes :address (recovery-address bytes)\n         :pack-bytes (:bytes e) :pack-address (:address e)\n         :root (:root e) :kind (:kind e)}))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Rehydrate: the fenced recovery\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- invalid!\n  [data]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Invalid export recovery\" (merge {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable} data))))\n\n\n(defn- header-agrees?\n  \"The recovery's header is the custody the pack's root slot carries:\n   nil exactly for a fork; otherwise the slot's keys by kind (blocked or\n   parked: occurrence, arbitration, counter and origin; halted: origin),\n   a nil header value being an absent key, as the lift writes it.\"\n  [header baseline]\n  (if (nil? header)\n    (true? (:yin.k/fork baseline))\n    (let [ks (if (= :halted (:yin.k/kind baseline))\n               [:yin.k/origin]\n               [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin])]\n      (and (not (:yin.k/fork baseline))\n           (= (into {} (filter (comp some? val)) (select-keys header ks))\n              (select-keys baseline ks))))))\n\n\n(defn- counter?\n  [x]\n  (or (nil? x) (and (integer? x) (<= 0 x))))\n\n\n(defn- valid-state?\n  \"The recovery state fits the decoded task: one issue stamp per carried\n   wait, and one child state per carried install, recursively.\"\n  [task state]\n  (let [ss (:slots task)\n        installs (nth ss 12)\n        waits (nth ss 13)]\n    (and (map? state)\n         (contains? #{nil :running :exporting :ended} (:gate state))\n         (vector? (:issues state))\n         (= (count (:issues state)) (count waits))\n         (every? counter? (:issues state))\n         (counter? (:issued state))\n         (counter? (:origins state))\n         (map? (:children state))\n         (= (set (keys (:children state))) (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs))\n         (every? (fn [inst]\n                   (let [[mn _ _ _ child] (:slots inst)]\n                     (valid-state? child (get-in state [:children mn]))))\n                 installs))))\n\n\n(defn- carried-trees\n  \"{A #{tree}} every task of the decoded tree carries: the composition's\n   index as the prepare that published the pack saw it, restricted to the\n   carried segments, which is all a relift of the same tree reads.\"\n  [task]\n  (let [ss (:slots task)]\n    (reduce (fn [acc inst] (merge acc (carried-trees (nth (:slots inst) 4))))\n            (or (:yin.k/trees (nth ss 10)) {})\n            (nth ss 12))))\n\n\n(defn- extract-recovered\n  \"The fenced machine and its export record from the lower's fenced\n   restore of one task: the waits and parked records the lower kept out\n   of the scheduler move into the record, the waits restamped with the\n   recovered issues; the holder-local counters come from `state`.\"\n  [machine state]\n  (let [children (into {}\n                       (map (fn [[module-name install]]\n                              [module-name\n                               (extract-recovered (:vm install)\n                                                  (get-in state [:children module-name]))]))\n                       (:installs machine))\n        waits (mapv (fn [entry issue]\n                      (if (some? issue)\n                        (assoc entry :yin.k/issue issue)\n                        (dissoc entry :yin.k/issue)))\n                    (:yin.k/recovery-waits machine)\n                    (:issues state))\n        record {:wait-set waits\n                :parked (or (:yin.k/recovery-parked machine) {})\n                :recovered? true\n                :gate (:gate state)\n                :served {}\n                :children (into {} (map (fn [[module-name recovered]]\n                                          [module-name (:record recovered)]))\n                                children)}\n        fenced (reduce-kv (fn [parent module-name recovered]\n                            (assoc-in parent [:installs module-name :vm]\n                                      (:machine recovered)))\n                          (cond-> (-> machine\n                                      (dissoc :yin.k/recovery-waits :yin.k/recovery-parked\n                                              :yin.k/custody :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued :origins)\n                                      (assoc :wait-set [] :parked {} :yin.k/gate :exporting))\n                            (some? (:origins state)) (assoc :origins (:origins state))\n                            (some? (:issued state)) (assoc :yin.k/issued (:issued state)))\n                          children)]\n    {:machine fenced :record record}))\n\n\n(defn rehydrate-fenced\n  \"Restore a version-2 export-recovery object into fresh receiver-owned\n   values (UCF 7.7.4).  Before any attachment: the object's tag and\n   version (`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`), its bytes against `address`\n   (`:yin.k/hash-mismatch`), the pack through the rows inspector (its\n   address against its bytes, the carrier, the custody grammar), the pack\n   root against the object's, the header against the root's custody\n   slot, and the state against the carried tree (any of these\n   `:yin.k/undecodable`, or the inspector's own refusal).  Then\n   `rows/lower-task {:fenced true}` over `receiver`, `attach` once per\n   stream identity: every task stays exporting, its waits and parked\n   records outside the scheduler and in the record, its id counter\n   exact; no program code runs, no stream is read, written, minted or\n   closed, no install child initializes.  Never restores tenure,\n   custody, scheduler waits or a runnable gate.  Last, the recovered\n   record is prepared again from what was attached and must encode the\n   published pack byte for byte, or the answer is `:yin.k/undecodable`\n   with `:yin.k/reason :recovery-inconsistent`.  Answers `{:status :ok\n   :machine m :record r}`, `r` marked `:recovered?` (abort refuses it).\"\n  [receiver recovery-bytes {:keys [address attach]}]\n  (try\n    (let [recovery (cbor/decode recovery-bytes)]\n      (cond\n        (not (and (map? recovery)\n                  (true? (:yin.k/export-recovery recovery))\n                  (integer? (:yin.k/version recovery))\n                  (= 2 (:yin.k/version recovery))))\n        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/profile-mismatch}\n\n        (not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address recovery-bytes))\n        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/hash-mismatch}\n\n        :else\n        (let [pack-bytes (jing/base64->bytes (:yin.k/pack-bytes recovery))\n              header (:yin.k/header recovery)\n              state (:yin.k/state recovery)\n              baseline (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/pack-address recovery) pack-bytes)\n              _ (when (:yin.k/status baseline) (invalid! baseline))\n              wire (cbor/decode pack-bytes)\n              task (rows/decode wire)\n              _ (when-not (= (:yin.k/root recovery) (:yin.k/root baseline))\n                  (invalid! {:yin.k/reason :root}))\n              _ (check-header! header)\n              _ (when-not (header-agrees? header baseline)\n                  (invalid! {:yin.k/reason :header}))\n              _ (when-not (valid-state? task state)\n                  (invalid! {:yin.k/reason :state}))\n              attached (atom {})\n              restored (rows/lower-task\n                         receiver wire\n                         (fn [descriptor]\n                           (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity descriptor)]\n                             (if (contains? @attached identity)\n                               (:answer (get @attached identity))\n                               (let [answer (attach descriptor)]\n                                 (swap! attached assoc identity {:answer answer :descriptor descriptor})\n                                 answer))))\n                         {:fenced true})\n              {:keys [machine record]} (extract-recovered restored state)\n              ;; each attached handle answers the descriptor it was served under\n              by-handle (into {}\n                              (map (fn [{:keys [answer descriptor]}]\n                                     [(:dao.stream/handle answer)\n                                      (select-keys descriptor [:dao.stream/identity\n                                                               :dao.stream/channel])]))\n                              (vals @attached))\n              prepared (prepare machine record #(get by-handle %) header (carried-trees task))\n              reproduced (when (= :ok (:status prepared))\n                           (encode machine (:record prepared)))]\n          (if (and (= :ok (:status reproduced))\n                   (= (vec pack-bytes) (vec (:bytes reproduced))))\n            {:status :ok :machine machine :record (assoc (:record prepared) :recovered? true)}\n            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable\n             :yin.k/reason :recovery-inconsistent}))))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) failure\n      (or (when (:yin.k/status (ex-data failure)) (ex-data failure))\n          {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable}))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Abort\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- not-appended?\n  \"True when `outcome`, the answer of an offer attempt's append, proves\n   the value was not appended.  `dao.stream`'s closed append outcome\n   set is {ok full invalid-value closed refused transport-error}: the\n   four refusals prove it; `ok` proves the opposite, and\n   `transport-error` stays the unknown-delivery refusal, as does no\n   answer.\"\n  [outcome]\n  (contains? #{:dao.stream/full :dao.stream/invalid-value\n               :dao.stream/closed :dao.stream/refused}\n             outcome))\n\n\n(defn abort\n  \"Return the exporting `machine` to local execution from `record`.\n\n   `attempts` is the offer-attempt history the composition persisted:\n   one map per attempt whose intent was durable before the send, with\n   `:append` the outcome its append answered (absent when none did).\n   Abort is legal when there is no attempt, or when every attempt's\n   append proves the value was not appended; anything else, including\n   an authority's refusal of one attempt, leaves the source fenced.  A\n   recovered record (`rehydrate-fenced`) is refused `:restarted`: a\n   restart never hands execution back.\n\n   A machine under custody (`:yin.k/custody`) is a holder exporting a\n   successor: it may abort only with `tenure`, `{:now n :bound b :live\n   true}`: `n` before `b` in one unit, and `:live` the ledger reader's\n   evidence that this lease is the occurrence's active lease at its\n   epoch.  A clock reading alone is not tenure.  After the lease has\n   ended its old local machine is never restored.\n\n   Answers `{:status :ok :machine m}` or `:yin.k/refused` data with\n   reason `:restarted`, `:not-exporting`, `:tenure-ended` (at or past\n   the bound), `:tenure-unconfirmed` (no ledger evidence) or\n   `:offer-possibly-accepted`.\"\n  [machine record attempts tenure]\n  (cond\n    (:recovered? record)\n    (refused :restarted)\n\n    (not= :exporting (vm/gate-mode machine))\n    (refused :not-exporting)\n\n    (and (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n         (some? (:now tenure))\n         (some? (:bound tenure))\n         (>= (:now tenure) (:bound tenure)))\n    (refused :tenure-ended)\n\n    (and (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n         (not (and (some? (:now tenure))\n                   (some? (:bound tenure))\n                   (true? (:live tenure)))))\n    (refused :tenure-unconfirmed)\n\n    (not (every? (comp not-appended? :append) attempts))\n    (refused :offer-possibly-accepted)\n\n    :else\n    (let [m (reinstated machine record)\n          prior (:gate record)]\n      {:status :ok\n       :machine (if (some? prior)\n                  (assoc m :yin.k/gate prior)\n                  (dissoc m :yin.k/gate))})))","numLines":628,"startLine":1,"totalLines":629}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013sQg2vbAsGa1n5MQP2Vfty","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
