e `Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)` marker/reason as elsewhere. |\n| F2 | continuation.md:715-716 | \"The fallback … lives only until phase 8.\" The register layout is a retained backend's layout, so this implies it goes away at phase 8. | Either \"remains a diagnostic extension of the retained register backend (§4.6)\", or state explicitly what changes at phase 8, if anything. |\n| F3 | continuation.md:1441-1442 | \"Until phase 8, a de Bruijn receiver refuses such a value…\" implies the refusal ends at phase 8. Since the backends are kept on the same fragment, it does not. | Drop \"Until phase 8,\" and add \"(retained after phase 8, §4.6)\". |\n| F4 | continuation.md:996-1001 (§4.6) | §4.6 names only row 4 as an exclusion the harness enforces rather than `lower-defect`. But `lower-defect` (`layout.cljc:916-948`) has just four clauses: image collision, installs, free-env value, and register payload prims. Only install rows 10-12 are refused by it before attach. The link-wait rows 7-9 and the module-context row 17 are also kept out only by the harness, and nothing in `layout/lower-task` refuses them before `rows/lower-task` attaches. Read together with UCF:2905-2906 (\"required to refuse the unsupported remainder before attach (continuation design §4.6)\"), §4.6 overstates how much of the remainder is gated. | Reword: \"Of the excluded rows, only the install rows 10-12 are refused before attach (`lower-defect` `:installs`); rows 4, 7-9 and 17 are excluded by the harness only, not by a general pre-attach fragment gate (§11 6c Q2).\" Optionally record the missing gate as an open item beside 6c Q2. |\n| F5 | UCF.md:3243-3245 (7.11.1 clause 1) | \"Fixtures … or corrupt a child task's profile\" with \"Stage: C inspector fixtures (7a)\". `rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc` has fixtures for version-float (`cbor/float64 3`), version-2, version-absent and no-tag, but none for a child-profile corruption. | Either drop \"or corrupt a child task's profile\" or mark it as an outstanding