{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016NsZfTXbSRdJXyFhKysjDQ","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e/collab/1792540000000-review-7e-docs.findings.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24e59ef2-1e11-40bc-bf74-9b03c65bd1ca","uuid":"a796d1c7-c35a-47cc-8175-7c2079919dbc","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:48:46.220Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7e/collab/1792540000000-review-7e-docs.findings.md","content":"Created-Local: 2026-10-14 +07\n# Review: slice 7e documentation checked against the code (opus, read-only)\n\nCommit reviewed: `32a98db1` on `srvm-phase7e`. Diff: `git diff srvm-phase7..HEAD` over the three design docs.\nCode read: `rows.cljc` (custody-keys, check-root-custody!, task-ops, custody-baseline, pack, pack-address, lift-task*, header-custody, protect!, lift-task, check-install!, check-pendings!, check-dependencies!, accept-grant!, check-custody!, with-custody, spawn-child, restore-task, lower-task), `rows/checkpoint.cljc` (inspect-pack), `holder/export.cljc` (whole file), `holder/driver.cljc` (export-fence-step, offer-request, grant :checkpoint, source-index seam), `compose.cljc` (source-index check, holder-config-keys, driver-config), `semantic_register/layout.cljc` (lower-defect, lower-task), and `rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`.\n\n## Verified true (no action)\n\n- Fork custody is nil on every row. `header-custody` with `custody-keys` gives the five-key slot by kind. A halted root takes origin only, and a header-bearing halt without origin refuses `:missing-header`. Children must be nil (`:child-header`) and are checked in the root's context (`task-ops`). These match continuation §2.5/§2.6, tuples §5.5 and UCF §7.7.4.\n- Lift order (continuation §7.1 step 10, tuples §9, UCF §7.7.4):\n  1. `lift-task*`, with `validate-frames`.\n  2. Exhaustion at `max-exact` (2^52-1) on non-halted roots.\n  3. `protect!` (`:unprotected-pending` / `:yin.k/unsatisfied`).\n  4. The slot is written.\n  5. `custody-baseline`.\n  6. `emit`.\n\n  `pack` sorts rows by `(str id)`.\n- `pack-address` is `jing/segment-key` of the wire (BLAKE3 by default), which is different from `:yin.k/root`. The baseline carries `:yin.k/root` (`inspect-pack`). The grant `:checkpoint` is compared to `pack-address` (`accept-grant!`). The offer `:yin.k/id` is the pack address.\n- Lower has three per-tree stages (`check-stores!`, `check-pendings!`, `check-dependencies!`), then `check-custody!` runs once, then `attach-streams!`. The custody table row matches `accept-grant!`'s checks and refusal statuses. `:fenced` skips `accept-grant!` (protection included), but the grammar and the `:exclusive` fork refusal still run.\n- `check-install!` checks: non-nil parent = `:yin.link/id` (`:install-link-id`); derivation `segment-key` = manifest `[:yin.module/derivations :yin.semantic/code]`; input = `:yin.module/tree`; output = `segment-key` of `(:value image)` (`:install-image`). The docs' \"self-consistency, no independent claimed-image-address check\" framing is accurate.\n- Fenced restore: every task is gated `:exporting`; waits go to `:yin.k/recovery-waits` and parked records to `:yin.k/recovery-parked`; the id counter is exact; `:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids` is set. `spawn-child` nils `:make-stream` and then restores it. Ordinary resume uses `max(local, carried)`.\n- Recovery format 2 keys exactly match `freeze`: tag, version 2, pack-address, root, pack-bytes base64, header, and state `{:gate :origins :issued :issues :children}`.\n- `rehydrate-fenced` checks the following before lower: tag/version, recovery address, inspector, root, header-agrees, valid-state. It then requires byte-identical re-encode and marks `:recovered?`. `abort` refuses `:restarted`, and custody is dissoc'd.\n- Driver order is recovery object, then pack, then the `:yin.k/fenced` journal record (`export-fence-step`). That matches tuples §7's \"after recovery format 2 and before journaling the fence\".\n- Source index is checked as a fn on `compose/open!`. It is a composition seam that `holder-config-keys` refuses. It is forwarded by `driver-config` and read by the driver. `export-version` appears nowhere in `src/`.\n- The three owner-approved UCF §7.11 edits are present:\n  - The backends are checked on a documented fragment (UCF:2902-2907).\n  - \"the canonical kernel and its two backends\" (UCF:3071).\n  - The pointer to continuation §4.6, which exists at continuation:991.\n- Cross-references resolve: continuation §2.5, §2.6, §4.1-4.4, §4.6, §5.3, §6.1, §7.1, §7.2, §10.8, §11; tuples §5.4, §5.5, §7, §8, §9; UCF §7.7.4, §7.11, §7.11.1.\n- Equal-baseline variant: the same root in another row order, while an id-counter change is `:variant-conflict`. This is stated consistently in continuation §11, tuples §7 and UCF 7.11.1 clause 10.\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | file:line | issue | correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | continuation.md:575 and :2541 (R1 row) | These still say the kernels are deleted at phase 8: \"editing both kernels' offset tables for a phase-8 deletion was not worth a slice\". That contradicts the owner ruling and §4.6. | Replace with \"editing both kernels' offset tables is outside the retained backend fragment (§4.6)\" and add the `Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)` marker/reason as elsewhere. |\n| F2 | continuation.md:715-716 | \"The fallback … lives only until phase 8.\" The register layout is a retained backend's layout, so this implies it goes away at phase 8. | Either \"remains a diagnostic extension of the retained register backend (§4.6)\", or state explicitly what changes at phase 8, if anything. |\n| F3 | continuation.md:1441-1442 | \"Until phase 8, a de Bruijn receiver refuses such a value…\" implies the refusal ends at phase 8. Since the backends are kept on the same fragment, it does not. | Drop \"Until phase 8,\" and add \"(retained after phase 8, §4.6)\". |\n| F4 | continuation.md:996-1001 (§4.6) | §4.6 names only row 4 as an exclusion the harness enforces rather than `lower-defect`. But `lower-defect` (`layout.cljc:916-948`) has just four clauses: image collision, installs, free-env value, and register payload prims. Only install rows 10-12 are refused by it before attach. The link-wait rows 7-9 and the module-context row 17 are also kept out only by the harness, and nothing in `layout/lower-task` refuses them before `rows/lower-task` attaches. Read together with UCF:2905-2906 (\"required to refuse the unsupported remainder before attach (continuation design §4.6)\"), §4.6 overstates how much of the remainder is gated. | Reword: \"Of the excluded rows, only the install rows 10-12 are refused before attach (`lower-defect` `:installs`); rows 4, 7-9 and 17 are excluded by the harness only, not by a general pre-attach fragment gate (§11 6c Q2).\" Optionally record the missing gate as an open item beside 6c Q2. |\n| F5 | UCF.md:3243-3245 (7.11.1 clause 1) | \"Fixtures … or corrupt a child task's profile\" with \"Stage: C inspector fixtures (7a)\". `rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc` has fixtures for version-float (`cbor/float64 3`), version-2, version-absent and no-tag, but none for a child-profile corruption. | Either drop \"or corrupt a child task's profile\" or mark it as an outstanding fixture. |\n| F6 | UCF.md:3248-3249 (clause 2) | \"extra keys (including current lease, epoch or holder)\": the fixtures cover `custody-epoch` and `custody-lease` but not holder. The code would refuse it (`:custody-key`), but the claimed fixture is absent. | Say \"(e.g. current lease or epoch)\", or add a holder fixture in a test slice. |\n| F7 | UCF.md:3506-3507 (clause 10) | \"Recovery format 2 is stored before the whole pack, both fenced before publication.\" The objects are not \"fenced\"; the fence is a journal record written after both stores. | \"Recovery format 2 is stored before the whole pack; both are stored durably before the fence is journaled and before any offer.\" |\n| F8 (low, unamended) | UCF.md:~2305 (\"The driver's exit persists recovery and body, journals the fence…\") and continuation.md:2509 (§10.6 D3 row: \"non-nil is `:yin.k/unsupported :custody`\") | Stale vocabulary next to amended text: \"body\" should be \"pack\", and the D3 row describes custody behaviour that 7a superseded. | \"persists the recovery object and the pack\"; append \"superseded by §10.8 P1\" to the D3 row's why-cell. |\n\nNothing else in the amended clauses was found false. In particular, no amended sentence claims that de Bruijn kernels are deleted at phase 8; only the unamended F1-F3 residues do.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016NsZfTXbSRdJXyFhKysjDQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
