{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzjfanHZARBbUCDodpn2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed the 7e docs against the code, and the verdict is **CHANGES_REQUESTED**. Everything needed is a small wording fix; I found no problem in the code.\n\nThe findings are in `collab/1792540000000-review-7e-docs.findings.md`. I edited nothing else and ran no tests, as the brief asked.\n\n**What checks out:** the rest of the amended clauses match the code, including the specific checks you listed:\n- Fork custody is nil on every row; exclusive custody uses only the five allowed keys, set by kind.\n- Lift and lower run in the order the docs give, and the install checks are as implemented.\n- Fenced recovery and the exact keys of recovery format 2 match `holder/export.cljc`.\n- Pack address and root id are separate, and the root is in the baseline.\n- An equal-baseline variant is the same root in another row order; an id-counter change is a `:variant-conflict`.\n- The driver stores the recovery object, then the pack, then journals the fence.\n- The `:source-index` seam is supplied by the composition and holders can't override it; `export-version` is gone.\n- All three owner-approved UCF 7.11 edits are present, and continuation §4.6 exists.\n- Section cross-references resolve.\n\n**What needs fixing:**\n1. **Kernels still \"deleted at phase 8\".** Two unamended sentences say so: continuation.md:575 and the R1 row at :2541 (\"for a phase-8 deletion\"). Two more imply something ends at phase 8: :716 (the register-layout fallback \"lives only until phase 8\") and :1442 (\"Until phase 8, a de Bruijn receiver refuses…\").\n2. **§4.6 overstates the pre-attach refusal.** It names only row 4 as kept out by the harness alone. In the code (`lower-defect`), only the install rows 10-12 are refused before attach. The link-wait rows 7-9 and the module-context row 17 are also kept out only by the harness. This matters because the owner-approved UCF 7.11 sentence points to §4.6 for \"refuse the unsupported remainder before attach\".\n3. **UCF 7.11.1 clauses 1 and 2 claim test fixtures that don't exist.** There is none for a corrupted child-task profile, and none for a current holder in the custody slot.\n4. **UCF 7.11.1 clause 10** says the recovery object and pack are \"both fenced\". In fact both are stored before the fence is journaled; the fence is a journal record, not something applied to the objects.\n5. **Two leftover old terms (low priority):** UCF still says the driver \"persists recovery and body\" (should be \"pack\"), and the continuation's §10.6 D3 row describes custody behaviour that phase 7a replaced.\n\nThe findings file gives the exact replacement text for each."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4812,"cache_read_input_tokens":126541,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4812},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24e59ef2-1e11-40bc-bf74-9b03c65bd1ca","uuid":"97d67b96-53aa-478a-be1a-6c7abf2b860b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T18:48:55.882Z","request_id":"req_011Cfzjfa67uj4hafLffdDoY"}
